## How the payment step works

If your application requires a fee, you'll be sent to a payment gateway to pay by card. After
paying, you're returned to a confirmation screen showing your transaction ID, a masked card
number, the amount, and a status.

## Payment statuses

- **Not started** — you haven't reached or completed the payment step yet.
- **Pending** — the payment is being processed. This is normal immediately after paying; it isn't
  a failure, and you don't need to pay again.
- **Paid** — the payment has been confirmed.

Online card payments are only ever set to "paid" by the payment gateway confirming the
transaction — an admissions officer can mark other payment methods as paid manually, but can't
do that for a card payment still shown as pending. If your status has been stuck on pending for an
unusually long time, contact the admissions office with your transaction ID rather than re-paying.

